===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An activity designed to give [[pleasure]], [[enjoyment]], [[diversion]], [[amusement]], or [[relaxation]] to an [[audience]], no matter whether the audience participates passively as in watching [[opera]] or a [[movie]], or actively as in [[game]]s.
#: {{syn|en|fare}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=The delinquents are generally the adventurous type, who have little use for reading and other non-active '''entertainment'''.|title=[[S:Roth v. United States/Dissent Douglas|Roth v. United States]]|author=William O. Douglas|year=1957}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=cyQFBOUHkaoC&pg=PA848&dq=%22need-nots%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwingP_849LMAhVD8WMKHR_FCgA4HhDoAQhGMAk#v=onepage&q=%22need-nots%22&f=false|title=Baxter's Practical Works, Volume 1: A Sum of Practical Theology, and Cases ...
|passage=Such abundance must be laid out on superfluous recreations, buildings, ornaments, furniture, equipage, attendants, '''entertainments''', visitations, braveries, and a world of need-nots {{...}}}}
# A [[show]] put on for the [[enjoyment]] or [[amusement]] of others.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[maintenance|Maintenance]] or [[support]].
#* {{quote-book|en|passage="This," said the matronly presence, ushering me into a low room on the right, "is where the Travellers sit by the fire, and cook what bits of suppers they buy with their fourpences."<br>"O! Then they have no '''Entertainment'''?" said I. For the inscription over the outer door was still running in my head, and I was mentally repeating, in a kind of tune, "Lodging, '''entertainment''', and fourpence each."|title=[[S:The Seven Poor Travellers|The Seven Poor Travellers]]|author=Charles Dickens|year=1854?<!--The year is estimated based on its appearance on Google books search.-->}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} An [[admission]] into [[service]]; a [[service]].
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=He must think us some band of strangers i' the adversary's '''entertainment'''.|author=William Shakespeare|title=[[S:All's Well That Ends Well|All's Well That Ends Well]]|year=1601-1608}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The [[payment]] of [[soldier]]s or [[servant]]s; [[wage]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1612|author={{w|John Davies (poet)|John Davies}}|title=Discoverie of the True Causes why Ireland was never entirely subdued
|passage=The '''entertainment''' of the general upon his first arrival was but six shillings and eight pence.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[reception]]; a ([[provision]] of) [[food]] to [[guest]]s or [[traveller]]s.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare As You Like It|II|4|text=I prithee, shepherd, if that love or gold<br>Can in this desert place buy '''entertainment''',<br>Bring us where we may rest ourselves and feed.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1743|author={{w|Robert Drury (sailor)|Robert Drury}}|title=The Pleasant, and Surprizing Adventures of Mr. Robert Drury, during his Fifteen Years Captivity on the Island of Madagascar|url=https://archive.org/details/pleasantandsurp00drurgoog|page=61|location=London
|passage=Tho’ they cut [the beef] into long Pieces, (like Ropes) with the Hide; and dress’d, and eat it half-roasted according to their Custom, and gave it me in the same Manner; yet I thought this contemptible Food, and what a Beggar in ''England'' would not have touch’d, the most delicious '''Entertainment''' I ever met with.}}

